# Decision Trees

## Definition

A Decision Tree is a supervised learning algorithm that recursively splits the data into subsets.

---

# Structure

- Root node
- Internal nodes
- Branches
- Leaf nodes

---

# Entropy

$$
Entropy=-\sum p_i\log_2p_i
$$

---

# Information Gain

$$
IG=Entropy(parent)-WeightedEntropy(children)
$$

---

# Gini Index

$$
Gini=1-\sum p_i^2
$$

Lower Gini indicates better purity.

---

# Advantages

- Easy interpretation
- Handles nonlinear data
- No feature scaling

---

# Disadvantages

- Overfitting
- High variance
- Sensitive to small data changes

---

# Pruning

## Pre-pruning

Stop growing early.

## Post-pruning

Grow completely then remove unnecessary branches.

---

# Applications

- Credit scoring
- Medical diagnosis
- Customer segmentation

---

# Exam Points

- Non-parametric
- White-box model
- Supports classification and regression
